  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Macrobrachium eriocheirum is a shrimp species received from Thailand. It reaches a body length of about 5 cm, making it one of the smaller species of the genus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Thailand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Regarding water chemistry the species is completely undemanding.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>The shrimps are omnivorous, but prefer meat when possible.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>They can be quite quarrelsome towards fish, so one has to think twice before placing them in a community tank.</p><p>Like chameleons, the shrimps alter their colours depending on the environment, so coloration can vary a lot.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males can be recognized by their unequal claws (scissor arms), which are very hairy.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_eriocheirum_en/",
      "html": "<p>M. eriocheirum belongs to the species with a more highly developed breeding behaviour. This means that its whole life cycle takes place in pure fresh water. In contrast to other Macrobrachium, the larvae do not have to grow up in the sea. So it is relatively easy to breed under aquarium conditions.</p>"
    }
  ],
